                        "entry_id": "dd867b48-3a09-32af-9109-052c0149eab5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To underestimate, or assign too low a value to (something or someone); to have too little regard for."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "728b138e-0e1d-483a-8f07-826c2b8060cb",
                                "sense_id": "6b80bd72-a1df-3092-91a3-20243f7f9ada",
                                "text": "Near-synonyms: underrate, underappreciate, underween"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f750bf84-bbfe-4b91-95e5-966be629b779",
                                "sense_id": "6b80bd72-a1df-3092-91a3-20243f7f9ada",
                                "text": "I write not this with the leaſt intention to undervalue the other parts of Poetry: for Comedy is both excellently inſtructive, and extreamly pleaſant: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b1c5adc-a678-4dfd-8bec-c1e984bd768c",
                                "sense_id": "6b80bd72-a1df-3092-91a3-20243f7f9ada",
                                "text": "[…] I undervalu'd all the Enſigns of Authority which belong'd to me, all the Pomp and Splendor of Life which^([sic – meaning with]) which I was ſurrounded."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
